# Immersive effects (sas-site)

Full guide: [docs/immersive-effects.md](../../docs/immersive-effects.md); non-WebGL motion systems (scroll reveal, route transitions): [docs/animations.md](../../docs/animations.md) — same defaults contract (`src/shared/ui/scroll-reveal` exports `SCROLL_REVEAL_INTRO`, `SCROLL_REVEAL_UNDER_MEDIA`, and `SCROLL_REVEAL_TRIGGER_DEFAULTS`). Shader technique lives in the **creative-webgl-shaders** skill; this rule is the project contract around it.

## Single source of truth — hard rules

- **Every tunable number exists once.** Each effect exports `<NAME>_DEFAULTS` (`as const satisfies Partial<Props>`) next to its props type; the component's destructured defaults AND the playground's leva `value:`s read from it. Never retype the number.
- **Internal shader layers own their numbers.** `RayMarchedHeading` / `RaymarchedSdfHeading` export their own `*_DEFAULTS`; wrappers (`TextLoadIn`, `TextLoadInRaymarched`) reference them — never restate.
- **Presets are delta-only.** `src/features/immersive/presets.ts` holds named shipped looks (e.g. `HERO_LENS`) containing only props that differ from the component defaults. Never restate a default in a preset, consumer, or playground.
- **Rule of two.** Tuning used once → inline props at the call site. Needed in a second place → promote to a named preset and import it from both. Never copy a prop bag between files.
- **Barrel-only imports.** Consumers import from `@/features/immersive` — never deep-import `…/immersive/ui/*`.
- Demo-only leva metadata (`min`/`max`/`step`/`label`) stays in playgrounds — it is curation, not component truth. Deliberate demo deviations from defaults stay literal with a `// demo-curated` comment.
- Content (copy, media src, layouts) always comes from the consumer; effects and presets never own content.

## When adding an effect

Follow the checklist in [docs/immersive-effects.md](../../docs/immersive-effects.md): component + `*_DEFAULTS` → barrel export → playground wired to the defaults → register in `immersive-demo-page.tsx`.

## What not to build

No registries, config providers, HOCs, or theme systems around effect tuning — props + exported objects are the whole mechanism. Don't merge effects that use different techniques (mip-blur smear vs true SDF raymarch stay separate).
